# Quarto
/.quarto/
/_site/
/_freeze/

# Local working notes, not part of the public site.
# The whole docs/ tree is maintainer-only: spec, plan, and handoff.
# _quarto.yml also excludes it from rendering via the project render allowlist.
/docs/
/CLAUDE.md
# Cross-model review reports (pi-review skill output): maintainer artifacts.
/quality_reports/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp

**/*.quarto_ipynb

# Local Python env for the validator (CI installs pyyaml directly)
/.venv/

# Agent tooling. The add-project skill ships with the repo; everything else under
# .claude/ is machine-local (worktrees, personal permission settings). Ignoring
# the directory's contents and re-including one child is the standard idiom, and
# it works because .claude/ itself is not excluded.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills/
